      "theorem_name": "RotationAndPowerReductionToPrimitiveValuationNecklaces",
      "declared_proposition": "For a positive valuation word a=(a0,...,a_(h-1)), let B(a) be its affine numerator and D=2^sum(a)-3^h. If rho(a) is the left cyclic rotation, then 2^a0 B(rho(a))=3B(a)+D; consequently D divides B(a) if and only if D divides B(rho(a)). If a=u^k, then B(a)=B(u)G and D(a)=D(u)G for the same positive geometric factor G. Every periodic integrality test therefore reduces exactly to a primitive cyclic valuation necklace.",
